## Section 3: Annotated Code Deconstruction

To demonstrate the implementation of this architecture, we present a complete Rust-based JIT compiler utilizing `cranelift-codegen` and `cranelift-jit` [3]. This compiler parses a basic declarative routing rule (e.g., "If the LLM confidence score stored at offset `0x10` is greater than or equal to `85`, route to Node A (offset `0x20` value `1`), otherwise route to Node B (offset `0x20` value `2`)") and compiles it into native machine instructions.

