## 3. Data Plane vs. Control Plane Protocol Dynamics

The separation of concerns between the high-frequency data plane (agent execution, message passing, tool invocation) and the control plane (actor placement, heartbeat monitoring, consensus) is critical for maintaining sub-millisecond local latency.

### Data Plane Wire Format and Serialization

To minimize serialization overhead and memory footprint within the high-frequency execution loop, we bypass standard JSON serialization in favor of **FlatBuffers** or **rkyv** for zero-copy deserialization. Below is the Protocol Buffers (v3) schema defining the high-performance gRPC streaming interface between the client, the orchestrator, and the tool execution sandbox:

```protobuf
syntax = "proto3";

package lola.orchestrator.v1;

service AgentOrchestrator {
  rpc StreamAgentSession(stream AgentClientMessage) returns (stream AgentServerMessage);
}

message AgentClientMessage {
  string agent_id = 1;
  string session_id = 2;
  uint64 sequence_number = 3;
  oneof payload {
    UserPrompt prompt = 4;
    ToolResult tool_response = 5;
  }
}

message UserPrompt {
  string text = 1;
  bytes context_metadata = 2;
}

message ToolResult {
  string tool_call_id = 1;
  int32 exit_code = 2;
  bytes stdout = 3;
  bytes stderr = 4;
}

message AgentServerMessage {
  string agent_id = 1;
  uint64 ack_sequence_number = 2;
  AgentStatus status = 3;
  oneof payload {
    AgentResponse response = 4;
    ToolInvocation tool_request = 5;
  }
}

enum AgentStatus {
  AGENT_STATUS_UNSPECIFIED = 0;
  AGENT_STATUS_IDLE = 1;
  AGENT_STATUS_THINKING = 2;
  AGENT_STATUS_EXECUTING_TOOL = 3;
  AGENT_STATUS_ERROR = 4;
}

message AgentResponse {
  string text = 1;
  bool is_final = 2;
}

message ToolInvocation {
  string tool_call_id = 1;
  string tool_name = 2;
  bytes arguments = 3; // Serialized FlatBuffer payload containing tool parameters
}
```

### Control Plane Consensus and State Machine Replication (SMR)

The control plane utilizes a Raft-backed consensus group to manage actor-to-node routing tables. When an agent session is initiated, the control plane registers the active host node in a distributed hash table (DHT). 

```
Sequence of Stateful Agent Execution Loop:

Client              Ingress Gateway          Orchestrator Node (Actor)         State Store / WAL
  |                        |                             |                             |
  |--- StreamAgentSession ->|
  |    (UserPrompt)        |                             |                             |
  |                        |------ Route(Agent ID) ----->|
  |                        |                             | (Lock Mailbox, Load State)  |
  |                        |                             |---------------------------->|
  |                        |                             |<-- Active State Snapshot ---|
  |                        |                             |                             |
  |                        |                             |-- Append WAL (State: Think) |
  |                        |                             |---------------------------->|
  |                        |                             |<------- WAL Append Ack -----|
  |                        |                             |                             |
  |                        |                             | [Execute Reasoning Loop]    |
  |                        |                             | [Spawn WASM Tool Sandbox]   |
  |                        |                             |                             |
  |                        |<-- ToolInvocation Stream ---|
  |<-- ToolInvocation -----|
```

